description:
The IPv4-mapped IPv6 normalization block (match client_ip { IpAddr::V6(v6) => v6.to_ipv4_mapped().map(IpAddr::V4).unwrap_or(IpAddr::V6(v6)), v4 => v4 }) is duplicated verbatim in two places:

- crates/smtp/src/session.rs:179-185 (production code in run_session)
- crates/smtp/src/config.rs:799-805 (test helper whitelist_check)

This violates DRY at a logic level, not just style. If the normalization rule changes (e.g., treating deprecated IPv4-compatible ::x.x.x.x addresses, or handling future IpAddr variants) the fix must be applied in two places. The comment explaining why to_ipv4_mapped() is preferred over to_ipv4() also needs to be duplicated.

Fix: extract to a free function, e.g. in crates/smtp/src/session.rs or a new crates/smtp/src/net_util.rs:

    pub(crate) fn normalize_client_ip(ip: IpAddr) -> IpAddr {
        match ip {
            IpAddr::V6(v6) => v6.to_ipv4_mapped().map(IpAddr::V4).unwrap_or(IpAddr::V6(v6)),
            v4 => v4,
        }
    }

Then both call sites use normalize_client_ip(client_ip). The whitelist_check test helper becomes a true exercise of the shared logic rather than a re-implementation.
